00:16:25.000 --> 00:16:28.920
So this is something
really cool about API.AI.

00:16:28.920 --> 00:16:32.040
You can very easily turn
this into a conversation

00:16:32.040 --> 00:16:37.080
where if I mark these three
parameters as required,

00:16:37.080 --> 00:16:39.570
I can now talk to
the user and ask

00:16:39.570 --> 00:16:42.660
it to fill the required fields.

00:16:42.660 --> 00:16:46.260
So if it's missing a
quantity, I can say,

00:16:46.260 --> 00:16:53.170
how many would you like to buy?

00:16:53.170 --> 00:16:59.140
And then for product, I can
ask, which product are you

00:16:59.140 --> 00:17:01.470
interested in?

00:17:01.470 --> 00:17:04.329
Notice that there's room
for multiple prompts.

00:17:04.329 --> 00:17:08.740
This is because we
found that sometimes you

00:17:08.740 --> 00:17:12.130
want to ask the same question
with multiple variations just

00:17:12.130 --> 00:17:16.119
to make it more
interesting for users.

00:17:16.119 --> 00:17:24.190
So let's also ask, where would
you like me to ship it to?

00:17:27.980 --> 00:17:29.580
And let's save this.

00:17:29.580 --> 00:17:30.860
And then let's try this again.

00:17:30.860 --> 00:17:36.270
Can I buy seven Chromecasts?

00:17:36.270 --> 00:17:38.870
OK, and so now you can
see it's responding.

00:17:38.870 --> 00:17:41.150
It says, where would you
like me to ship it to?

00:17:41.150 --> 00:17:48.200
And now I can tell it, 1
First Street, San Francisco,

00:17:48.200 --> 00:17:50.170
California.

00:17:50.170 --> 00:17:52.666
And then it responds,
adding seven Chromecasts

00:17:52.666 --> 00:17:54.040
and sending it to
1 First Street,

00:17:54.040 --> 00:17:56.290
San Francisco, California.

00:17:56.290 --> 00:18:01.110
OK, this is all good
and pretty awesome.

00:18:01.110 --> 00:18:03.820
Let's try one last one.

00:18:03.820 --> 00:18:06.620
And then make this a
little bit more complex.

00:18:06.620 --> 00:18:10.780
Let's try one that's
missing quantity.

00:18:10.780 --> 00:18:17.200
So I'd like to buy a few Pixels.

00:18:17.200 --> 00:18:19.790
Now, I never actually
trained it on a sentence

00:18:19.790 --> 00:18:22.460
that looks like that.

00:18:22.460 --> 00:18:24.350
If you look at the
other ones, there's

00:18:24.350 --> 00:18:26.780
no place where I say a few.

00:18:26.780 --> 00:18:31.530
But it already understands
that I want to do commerce.

00:18:31.530 --> 00:18:34.020
Actually, it didn't get
the product this time.

00:18:34.020 --> 00:18:35.490
We'll fix that in a second.

00:18:35.490 --> 00:18:38.789
But I guess it's
because of the few.

00:18:38.789 --> 00:18:40.080
How many would you like to buy?

00:18:40.080 --> 00:18:46.334
Let's give it eight
Pixel And where would you

00:18:46.334 --> 00:18:47.250
like me to ship it to?

00:18:47.250 --> 00:18:52.020
7 Seventh Street, San
Francisco, California.

00:18:52.020 --> 00:18:54.780
And now you can see it
finishes the full thing.

00:18:54.780 --> 00:19:01.110
So we can go back on
training and just tell it

00:19:01.110 --> 00:19:03.690
that if you have
something with few,

00:19:03.690 --> 00:19:09.290
that still is a legitimate ask.

00:19:14.500 --> 00:19:18.630
OK, so now let's make it a
little bit more interesting.

00:19:18.630 --> 00:19:25.170
Now, let's say
that you want to be

00:19:25.170 --> 00:19:28.716
able to feed this into
your back end application

00:19:28.716 --> 00:19:30.090
into some sort of
a shopping cart

00:19:30.090 --> 00:19:32.820
and be able to add
sort of multiple items

00:19:32.820 --> 00:19:35.190
from the same kind.

00:19:35.190 --> 00:19:38.580
So what I want to do here is
to have some sort of counter,

00:19:38.580 --> 00:19:43.220
where I send this counter
to my back end, my back end

00:19:43.220 --> 00:19:47.540
increments by one, and then
sends it back to API.AI

00:19:47.540 --> 00:19:48.840
with an answer.

00:19:48.840 --> 00:19:50.815
So the way I'm going
to do this is I'm

00:19:50.815 --> 00:19:52.440
going to create what
we call a context.

00:19:52.440 --> 00:19:56.860
So I'm going to create a
context called Shopping Cart.

00:19:56.860 --> 00:20:00.730
And now every time someone
does a commerce operation,

00:20:00.730 --> 00:20:03.070
it's going to save it
in the shopping cart.

00:20:03.070 --> 00:20:05.450
And I'm going to create
another intent that requires

00:20:05.450 --> 00:20:07.610
Shopping Cart as an input.

00:20:07.610 --> 00:20:12.610
So this will now only happen
if someone has a shopping cart.

00:20:12.610 --> 00:20:16.380
And let's say someone
says, please add one more

00:20:16.380 --> 00:20:25.540
or I'd like to buy another
one or another one, please.

00:20:25.540 --> 00:20:27.100
Let's call this Buyanother.

00:20:32.250 --> 00:20:35.180
Buyanother.

00:20:35.180 --> 00:20:46.970
And now let's add from
Shopping Cart, the product.

00:20:52.830 --> 00:20:58.020
And let's add the quantity
and let's add the address.

00:21:02.750 --> 00:21:12.660
So number and address and
shopping cart quantity

00:21:12.660 --> 00:21:15.830
and shopping cart address.

00:21:20.820 --> 00:21:22.050
OK, let's save.

00:21:22.050 --> 00:21:23.880
Now, what I'm going
to do is I'm going

00:21:23.880 --> 00:21:26.780
to connect it to my WebHook.

00:21:29.197 --> 00:21:30.780
And if it doesn't
work, I'm just going

00:21:30.780 --> 00:21:33.120
to put error, so that we
know that it didn't actually

00:21:33.120 --> 00:21:35.310
go to the WebHook.

00:21:35.310 --> 00:21:39.730
And I just want to show you
guys how that looks like.

00:21:39.730 --> 00:21:41.340
So you can see,
this is a WebHook

00:21:41.340 --> 00:21:44.250
I created in Cloud
Functions earlier.

00:21:44.250 --> 00:21:46.680
That basically increments
one to a context

00:21:46.680 --> 00:21:48.702
that comes from API.AI.

00:21:48.702 --> 00:21:51.670
I can show you guys
the actual code.

00:21:51.670 --> 00:21:54.040
It's basically four
or five lines of code.

00:21:54.040 --> 00:21:55.100
That's all.

00:21:55.100 --> 00:21:59.010
And no JS, by the way,
if someone's interested.

00:21:59.010 --> 00:22:01.894
So let's try it out.

00:22:01.894 --> 00:22:02.810
Let's see if it works.

00:22:02.810 --> 00:22:11.290
So let's start by, I'd like
to buy a Chromebook, please.

00:22:11.290 --> 00:22:15.437
Let's make it two
Chromebooks, please.

00:22:15.437 --> 00:22:17.020
Where would you like
me to ship it to?

00:22:17.020 --> 00:22:22.910
Let's say, 7 Seventh
Street, San Francisco.

00:22:22.910 --> 00:22:23.965
So it's great.

00:22:23.965 --> 00:22:26.380
It responds that it's adding
it to my shopping cart.

00:22:26.380 --> 00:22:29.420
I get a context of
a shopping cart.

00:22:29.420 --> 00:22:33.910
And now let's ask
it for another one.

00:22:33.910 --> 00:22:35.690
And so you can see the response.

00:22:35.690 --> 00:22:37.460
Adding one more
Chromebook, you now

00:22:37.460 --> 00:22:41.120
have three in your
shopping cart.

00:22:41.120 --> 00:22:43.595
And remember the context
of a conversation

00:22:43.595 --> 00:22:45.860
that you have a Chromebook.

00:22:45.860 --> 00:22:48.860
It's sent it to our back
end, the back end incremented

00:22:48.860 --> 00:22:51.380
by one, sent it
back, and now you're

00:22:51.380 --> 00:22:53.975
seeing the response at three.

00:22:53.975 --> 00:22:59.012
If I try and trigger this
again, please add one more,

00:22:59.012 --> 00:23:01.220
you'll see it says you now
have four in your shopping

00:23:01.220 --> 00:23:03.290
cart of the Chromebooks.

00:23:03.290 --> 00:23:08.720
So what you see here is
I didn't measure time,

00:23:08.720 --> 00:23:10.670
but I think it's
something like 10,

00:23:10.670 --> 00:23:13.220
15 minutes, we basically
built this whole conversation

00:23:13.220 --> 00:23:13.720
application.

00:23:13.720 --> 00:23:14.680
It does commerce.

00:23:14.680 --> 00:23:16.110
It does service.

00:23:16.110 --> 00:23:18.590
It'll get better the more
we add more examples to it,

00:23:18.590 --> 00:23:21.560
the more it gets usage data,
and the more that we train it.

00:23:21.560 --> 00:23:24.440
But it can already handle a
lot of queries pretty easily.

00:23:24.440 --> 00:23:30.200
Now, what I would like to do
is I'm going to connect it here

00:23:30.200 --> 00:23:32.960
to Facebook Messenger.

00:23:32.960 --> 00:23:35.840
And you can see we have
one-click integrations.

00:23:35.840 --> 00:23:38.450
Like, very easy
to start and stop.

00:23:41.600 --> 00:23:44.220
Let's just start it.

00:23:44.220 --> 00:23:47.780
And I'm going to go
to Facebook Messenger.

00:23:47.780 --> 00:23:51.345
And now let's say, I'd like
to buy a Pixel, please.

00:23:55.510 --> 00:23:59.520
Obviously, it's not working.

00:23:59.520 --> 00:24:01.030
OK, perfect.

00:24:01.030 --> 00:24:03.134
How many would you like to buy?

00:24:03.134 --> 00:24:04.195
[APPLAUSE]

00:24:04.195 --> 00:24:05.236
Go ahead and tell it six.

00:24:09.500 --> 00:24:10.850
Thank you.

00:24:10.850 --> 00:24:12.290
Let's give it an address.

00:24:12.290 --> 00:24:17.990
6 6th Street, San
Francisco, California.

00:24:17.990 --> 00:24:19.910
And now let's try
the last thing,

00:24:19.910 --> 00:24:22.410
another one where it goes
directly to our WebHook.

00:24:22.410 --> 00:24:25.820
OK, now you can
say it says seven.

00:24:25.820 --> 00:24:27.500
So that's it, guys.

00:24:27.500 --> 00:24:30.797
[APPLAUSE]

00:24:34.387 --> 00:24:35.220
Thank you very much.

00:24:35.220 --> 00:24:37.870
We got through this together.

00:24:37.870 --> 00:24:43.960
You can see just how easy it
is to create a conversation

00:24:43.960 --> 00:24:45.910
application that's
really powerful.

00:24:45.910 --> 00:24:49.180
And with ease, you can
connect it automatically

00:24:49.180 --> 00:24:53.680
to all of those cross-platform
applications you saw earlier.

00:24:53.680 --> 00:24:55.330
You can put it on
your own website,

00:24:55.330 --> 00:24:59.560
in your own mobile
app, or work through it

00:24:59.560 --> 00:25:02.050
with the different messengers.

00:25:02.050 --> 00:25:03.530
Very, very exciting.

00:25:03.530 --> 00:25:05.860
So there'll be Q&amp;A later.

00:25:05.860 --> 00:25:09.670
But now I'd like to invite
to the stage Cornelius that

00:25:09.670 --> 00:25:11.620
is going to show us
a little bit more

00:25:11.620 --> 00:25:15.132
about what they've
done at Bosch.

00:25:15.132 --> 00:25:16.551
CORNELIUS MUNZ: Thanks.

00:25:16.551 --> 00:25:20.820
[APPLAUSE]

00:25:20.820 --> 00:25:22.480
So thanks, Dan.

00:25:22.480 --> 00:25:23.560
My name is Cornelius.

00:25:23.560 --> 00:25:26.960
I'm working at Bosch
Thermotechnology.

00:25:26.960 --> 00:25:32.950
We are Europe's leading OEM for
heating appliances, boilers,

00:25:32.950 --> 00:25:36.080
appliances who prepare
hot water for you.

00:25:36.080 --> 00:25:39.530
So can we switch
to the slide deck?

00:25:44.440 --> 00:25:45.350
Slide disk.

00:25:52.650 --> 00:25:55.090
OK, I go on.

00:25:55.090 --> 00:25:55.770
OK, thanks.

00:25:58.630 --> 00:26:02.450
OK, and our devices
become more and more

00:26:02.450 --> 00:26:03.620
smarter the last years.

00:26:03.620 --> 00:26:07.372
So we have now out of
the box IT connectivity

00:26:07.372 --> 00:26:09.130
are built in in our devices.

00:26:09.130 --> 00:26:12.750
Are if you sell a Bosch
appliance, a Bosch [INAUDIBLE],

00:26:12.750 --> 00:26:15.500
you will get out of
the box AIPI support.

00:26:15.500 --> 00:26:20.590
You can connect your app to
it and remote control it.

00:26:20.590 --> 00:26:21.640
So that's fine.

00:26:21.640 --> 00:26:23.050
But we have a problem.

00:26:23.050 --> 00:26:25.840
We lose the contact more
and more to the customer.

00:26:25.840 --> 00:26:29.530
So how get the interface
back to the customer

00:26:29.530 --> 00:26:32.320
if the device becomes
more and more smarter?

00:26:32.320 --> 00:26:34.930
And our approach
was that we tried

00:26:34.930 --> 00:26:38.530
to figure out how our
conversational bots can

00:26:38.530 --> 00:26:42.460
be used to keep in
contact to our devices.

00:26:42.460 --> 00:26:45.180
And how does it work?

00:26:45.180 --> 00:26:48.910
So we have had the answer
from a software architecture

00:26:48.910 --> 00:26:51.760
perspective, many for layers.

00:26:51.760 --> 00:26:54.490
On the left side, you
can see the interaction

00:26:54.490 --> 00:26:59.680
of the user integrated in Skype,
Slack, Facebook Messenger,

00:26:59.680 --> 00:27:02.120
whatever, your own home page.

00:27:02.120 --> 00:27:06.270
And the user can send the
message to the API.AI chatbot.

00:27:06.270 --> 00:27:11.650
That chatbot processes the
intent, as shown by Dan before,

00:27:11.650 --> 00:27:15.200
and the intent detection
fires then a HTTP call

00:27:15.200 --> 00:27:16.630
to the WebHook.

00:27:16.630 --> 00:27:20.050
And the WebHook is now a piece
of software we have developed,

00:27:20.050 --> 00:27:26.190
which maps the API.AI intent
to a domain-specific API call,

00:27:26.190 --> 00:27:28.540
so which will call
to our boiler.

00:27:28.540 --> 00:27:30.820
And the boiler
can, in that case,

00:27:30.820 --> 00:27:35.910
set a new room temperature
setpoint to a new value,

00:27:35.910 --> 00:27:38.680
respond with a HTTP, OK.

00:27:38.680 --> 00:27:42.370
And then we can prepare
a fulfillment message

00:27:42.370 --> 00:27:46.300
in our WebHook to respond
to the message of the user.

00:27:46.300 --> 00:27:49.150
API.AI then routes
that message back

00:27:49.150 --> 00:27:52.370
to the originated
messaging application.

00:27:52.370 --> 00:27:53.840
And then it's done.

00:27:53.840 --> 00:27:56.080
The boiler has set
a new temperature.

00:27:56.080 --> 00:28:01.240
And hopefully, the
user [INAUDIBLE].

00:28:01.240 --> 00:28:04.120
So let's have a
look on the demo.

00:28:04.120 --> 00:28:05.290
So back to the demo.

00:28:10.260 --> 00:28:13.780
So here I have a demo
set up on the left side.

00:28:13.780 --> 00:28:17.440
You can see our internet portal,
which is already available.

00:28:17.440 --> 00:28:20.560
So you can control
your heating appliance.

00:28:20.560 --> 00:28:24.420
Can set some values, for
example, the current room

00:28:24.420 --> 00:28:28.590
temperature setpoint,
the hot water setpoint

00:28:28.590 --> 00:28:30.630
for your shower and bath.

00:28:30.630 --> 00:28:33.470
And you can, for example,
prepare a holiday mode.

00:28:33.470 --> 00:28:37.710
If you are leaving the home,
the device is going to stand by.

00:28:37.710 --> 00:28:42.590
And you can save a lot
of money if the heating

00:28:42.590 --> 00:28:45.050
device is switched off.

00:28:45.050 --> 00:28:48.690
On the right side, I have
connected here my iPhone.

00:28:48.690 --> 00:28:50.020
And Skype is opened.

00:28:50.020 --> 00:28:53.580
And you see, like in the
demo before with the Facebook

00:28:53.580 --> 00:28:57.600
Messenger, you have a
bot us a chat contact.

00:28:57.600 --> 00:29:03.445
And then you can say, OK, for
example I will be on holiday.

00:29:06.960 --> 00:29:12.300
And I have used Siri to transfer
speech to a chat message.

00:29:12.300 --> 00:29:15.060
And then a required
parameter is missing.

00:29:15.060 --> 00:29:18.930
To call the API of the boiler,
I need the date period.

00:29:18.930 --> 00:29:22.130
And the bot asks me for that.

00:29:22.130 --> 00:29:25.300
Next week.

00:29:25.300 --> 00:29:27.770
I will send this next week.

00:29:27.770 --> 00:29:31.810
And the magic in API.AI
transfers from then next week

00:29:31.810 --> 00:29:35.520
in a date period, which could
be processed by our API.

00:29:35.520 --> 00:29:38.660
And next week, hopefully, yeah.

00:29:38.660 --> 00:29:41.140
it's transformed in a date.

00:29:41.140 --> 00:29:45.190
And if our portal works fine,
that we have to refresh it.

00:29:50.810 --> 00:29:55.060
Holiday mode is switched on
with the desired date period.

00:29:55.060 --> 00:29:56.620
And we are done.

00:29:56.620 --> 00:29:58.510
So use conversational--

00:29:58.510 --> 00:30:00.400
[APPLAUSE]

00:30:00.400 --> 00:30:07.800
--UX-- thanks-- to keep in
contact with your device.

00:30:07.800 --> 00:30:11.550
And that's a good
possibility for us.

00:30:11.550 --> 00:30:15.930
So let's dig a little bit
more into development issues.

00:30:15.930 --> 00:30:18.501
How do we have done this?

00:30:18.501 --> 00:30:23.060
It's the same setup we have
seen by [INAUDIBLE] before.

00:30:23.060 --> 00:30:24.580
We have different
use cases, so we

00:30:24.580 --> 00:30:26.840
can activate the holiday mode.

00:30:26.840 --> 00:30:30.130
You can set or get
the auto temperature.

00:30:30.130 --> 00:30:33.050
You can ask the boiler, if
you want to take a shower,

00:30:33.050 --> 00:30:36.870
if the hot water is
prepared, and so on.

00:30:36.870 --> 00:30:42.180
And you can set your schedule
