00:44:56.860 --> 00:44:58.300
Right.

00:44:58.300 --> 00:45:01.990
Let's go to the API.AI and
how we implemented this.

00:45:01.990 --> 00:45:05.350
So what I wanted
to show you and how

00:45:05.350 --> 00:45:08.730
we used to trigger the
conversational logic

00:45:08.730 --> 00:45:10.100
is like this.

00:45:10.100 --> 00:45:14.530
So say, where is my
card or something else.

00:45:14.530 --> 00:45:19.970
The JSON line you are
interested in is this one.

00:45:19.970 --> 00:45:21.700
So there is an action.

00:45:21.700 --> 00:45:25.310
And just using that action, you
can program anything manually

00:45:25.310 --> 00:45:28.060
for fulfillments for further on.

00:45:28.060 --> 00:45:30.790
But what is maybe
more interesting here,

00:45:30.790 --> 00:45:34.570
and I'm going to take you
to our development Marie,

00:45:34.570 --> 00:45:38.200
is that once your bots are
going to be scaled further

00:45:38.200 --> 00:45:41.920
and you are going to build
a lot of different intents

00:45:41.920 --> 00:45:45.940
and conversations,
it will get messy.

00:45:45.940 --> 00:45:47.170
It will be back and forth.

00:45:47.170 --> 00:45:52.240
And people will not just
follow the preprogrammed line.

00:45:52.240 --> 00:45:54.700
So you want to be
able to still navigate

00:45:54.700 --> 00:45:56.080
within that conversation.

00:45:56.080 --> 00:45:59.060
Now, one of the ways we
found, at least for ourselves,

00:45:59.060 --> 00:46:01.510
how you can do that in
API.AI is to create, first,

00:46:01.510 --> 00:46:03.010
some kind of a
naming convention,

00:46:03.010 --> 00:46:05.590
because otherwise
it's a big mess.

00:46:05.590 --> 00:46:08.550
And understand that
for one use case,

00:46:08.550 --> 00:46:11.060
there is actually many
intents which you can use.

00:46:11.060 --> 00:46:13.770
So say there is a use
case activate card,

00:46:13.770 --> 00:46:17.647
but one kind of a use
case is more intents

00:46:17.647 --> 00:46:18.730
which you want to trigger.

00:46:18.730 --> 00:46:21.120
So we're going to
start the first intent

00:46:21.120 --> 00:46:24.080
and then pass this context
up until the last one.

00:46:24.080 --> 00:46:26.890
So let's see how it looks.

00:46:26.890 --> 00:46:31.690
So you see that the first intent
has no input context, but just

00:46:31.690 --> 00:46:33.160
the output context.

00:46:33.160 --> 00:46:37.020
And then you want to pass
those along the conversation.

00:46:37.020 --> 00:46:38.320
Here are the [INAUDIBLE].

00:46:38.320 --> 00:46:40.540
Typically, you would put
hundreds of them, which we

00:46:40.540 --> 00:46:43.990
have in our to-be-live version.

00:46:43.990 --> 00:46:47.140
And then what is
also interesting

00:46:47.140 --> 00:46:50.830
here is managing
the conversation.

00:46:50.830 --> 00:46:57.220
So here we put the response
without a parameter and here

00:46:57.220 --> 00:46:58.916
with a parameter.

00:46:58.916 --> 00:47:01.180
