00:55:51.090 --> 00:55:53.480
a trivial connection?

00:55:53.480 --> 00:55:58.431
DAN AHARON: Yeah,
so their interfaces

00:55:58.431 --> 00:55:59.680
are slightly different, right?

00:55:59.680 --> 00:56:04.285
And so the data that they send
to other applications and back,

00:56:04.285 --> 00:56:05.660
the format is a
little different.

00:56:05.660 --> 00:56:09.070
But we've built our
connectors to try and minimize

00:56:09.070 --> 00:56:11.080
that sort of interruption
as much as possible,

00:56:11.080 --> 00:56:14.530
so that our developers can focus
on the actual conversational

00:56:14.530 --> 00:56:16.000
logic.

00:56:16.000 --> 00:56:19.210
So for the most part,
you can build one logic

00:56:19.210 --> 00:56:21.090
and connect it to
multiple connectors.

00:56:21.090 --> 00:56:22.402
AUDIENCE: It'll connect

00:56:22.402 --> 00:56:23.110
DAN AHARON: Yeah.

00:56:23.110 --> 00:56:27.970
Now, the caveat is when
you're talking to Google Home

00:56:27.970 --> 00:56:31.610
by voice versus
if you're texting

00:56:31.610 --> 00:56:34.090
on Google Allo or
Facebook Messenger,

00:56:34.090 --> 00:56:36.580
the users speak sometimes
in a different way,

00:56:36.580 --> 00:56:37.810
use different words.

00:56:37.810 --> 00:56:40.310
And the way you want to talk
back to them is also different.

00:56:40.310 --> 00:56:43.750
Like on a chat, you might want
to show them cards with a map

00:56:43.750 --> 00:56:48.325
or maybe you want to write
a long paragraph of text.

00:56:48.325 --> 00:56:50.500
When you're reading
back on Google Home,

00:56:50.500 --> 00:56:54.010
you don't want to read back
a long paragraph of text,

00:56:54.010 --> 00:56:55.990
because users will
get bored, right?

00:56:55.990 --> 00:56:58.047
So you actually
may want to build

00:56:58.047 --> 00:57:00.130
different conversational
experiences for each one.

00:57:00.130 --> 00:57:04.050
But if you wanted to create a
single experience, you could.

00:57:04.050 --> 00:57:06.610
CORNELIUS MUNZ: And from
a technical point of view,

00:57:06.610 --> 00:57:09.940
you have to make a trust
relation between Facebook

00:57:09.940 --> 00:57:11.560
and API.AI.

00:57:11.560 --> 00:57:14.830
And you would generate an
API key on Facebook or Skype

00:57:14.830 --> 00:57:20.890
or whatever and copy that API
key into the API.AI console.

00:57:20.890 --> 00:57:23.110
And that's all so a
trust relation is there.

00:57:23.110 --> 00:57:26.200
And then Skype
can talk to API.AI

00:57:26.200 --> 00:57:27.497
and respond to that message.

